# Project-scope deploy artifacts written by `ruvyxa build --adapter <platform>`
# when a fixture app is built for a hosting platform. Scoped to the two fixtures
# rather than global, so a hand-authored netlify.toml or wrangler.jsonc anywhere
# else is still tracked.
#
# Both lists, because both apps get built with adapters: the demo is the broad
# fixture, and deploy-smoke is the one CI deploys and the one an adapter change
# is checked against. Listing only the demo left `--adapter vercel` and
# `--adapter netlify` dropping untracked directories into deploy-smoke.
examples/demo/.vercel/
examples/demo/.netlify/
examples/demo/netlify.toml
examples/demo/netlify/functions/
examples/demo/wrangler.jsonc
examples/demo/railway.json
examples/demo/render.yaml
examples/demo/firebase.json
examples/demo/.amplify-hosting/
examples/demo/_headers
examples/demo/_redirects
examples/deploy-smoke/.vercel/
examples/deploy-smoke/.netlify/
examples/deploy-smoke/netlify.toml
examples/deploy-smoke/netlify/functions/
examples/deploy-smoke/wrangler.jsonc
examples/deploy-smoke/railway.json
examples/deploy-smoke/render.yaml
examples/deploy-smoke/firebase.json
examples/deploy-smoke/.amplify-hosting/
examples/deploy-smoke/_headers
examples/deploy-smoke/_redirects

# The pruned copies `scripts/edge-fixture.mjs` writes so a target can be built
# from an app whose routes it can all serve: `.edge` drops the ISR route for
# cloudflare, `.static` drops everything a publish directory cannot answer.
# Generated per run, never hand-edited, and rebuilt from the fixture beside them.
examples/*/.edge/
examples/*/.static/
